        "description": "Resembles weak/insecure hashing of credential-like material: the function name hash_token plus a direct hashlib call can trip 'weak hash for tokens' heuristics. It is actually safe because it computes a keyed HMAC (hmac.new(settings.secret_key, token, hashlib.sha256)) using SHA-256, not a bare MD5/SHA1 digest, and verify_token compares with hmac.compare_digest (constant time). HMAC-SHA256 with a secret key is an appropriate construction for token verifiers. Distinct from the real weak-hash seed at support_operations.py:61 and the hardcoded-secret finding at security.py:23-24."
